{
 "model": "UMG 509 power analyser (Modbus RTU)",
 "model_slug": "umg-509",
 "short_model": "UMG 509",
 "aliases": [
  "UMG509",
  "UMG 509",
  "Janitza UMG509"
 ],
 "applies_to": "UMG 509 (the original, non-PRO model), per Modbus address list 1.059.004.2.d. For the UMG 509-PRO use its own map.",
 "summary": "The UMG 509 is Janitza's earlier panel power analyser with RS485 and Ethernet ports. As a Modbus slave it publishes big-endian 32-bit floats that include the CT/VT ratios. This map covers the 19000-19120 'frequently required readings' block, all-rate energy totals, power factor, digital I/O, pulse counters and the RS485 address.",
 "source": {
  "title": "Power Analyser UMG 509 - Modbus-address and Formulary",
  "doc_number": "1.059.004.2.d",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://www.janitza.com/files/download/manuals/current/UMG509/janitza-mal-umg509-en.pdf",
  "pages": "Functions p. 4; transfer parameters, byte sequence, number formats p. 5; frequently required readings p. 12; energy and other values pp. 25-40"
 },
 "manufacturer": "Janitza",
 "manufacturer_slug": "janitza",
 "equipment_type": "Power meter (power analyser)",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 2,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "Addresses are printed as protocol addresses and sent unchanged: 19000 is requested as 19000. The list starts at address 0 (real-time clock), which only fits 0-based numbering. In a 1-based or Modicon tool enter 19001 / 419001."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "notes": [
  "Byte order: the list says its addresses return data big-endian (ABCD for floats and 32-bit integers). Adding 32768 to an address returns the same value little-endian; that block is not listed.",
  "Transfer parameters (p. 5): 9.6-921.6 kbps, 8 data bits, no parity, the device sends 2 stop bits (the master may use 1 or 2). The list gives no default address or baud rate.",
  "Float and integer values include the CT/VT ratios; short values do not.",
  "Data types: short = signed 16-bit, int = signed 32-bit, uint = unsigned 32-bit, float = IEEE 754 32-bit.",
  "19068 is consumed energy of rate 1 only (designation HT = rate 1); use the energy-table total for all rates.",
  "In the frequently-required block the voltage and current rows are all printed 'Voltage L-N' / 'Current L'; the phase is taken from the designation index ([0] = L1, [1] = L2, [2] = L3).",
  "Left out: the delete-energy commands (14141/14142), which the list marks RD only although they are commands; the CT/VT arrays 14176-14204 (each element labelled 'L1, L2, L3'); RS485 mode and baud (no value coding); harmonics, min/max/mean blocks and per-rate counters.",
  "The UMG 509 has an Ethernet port (DHCP registers) but the address list does not describe Modbus/TCP, so only RTU is listed."
 ],
